      "source": [
        "## 17. Compatibility Ledger (STACK vs ALTERNATIVE vs NEVER-SAME-PATH)",
        "",
        "Standing rule: every new technique/impl ships with a compatibility note - what it composes with, what it replaces (pick exactly 1), and what it is guaranteed incompatible with (never the same path). The job is to maximise guaranteed-good combos. This ledger is the current record; exclusion enforcement is future compiler work, until then this is the contract.",
        "",
        "**STACK (compose freely, different stages/sites).** Checkpoint probing (train-time) + any probe head + any aggregation rule; SABER exit gating (inference) + LayerMix probe scores; ConvMem hierarchy feeding generations that SABER early-exits (stages differ, expected compatible, untested combo); Corrupt eval sets + any probe head (data orthogonal to heads); grokking clocks + checkpoint probing (same-loop observers); extractor + everything (read-only hooks).",
        "",
        "**ALTERNATIVE (same site: pick exactly 1 per path/run).** Aggregation: layermix | singleoracle | alllayeravg. Probe head per decision: l2lr | fisherlda | shrinkagelda | plsda | svd | meandiff | mlp | 1d-lr. SABER scoring: RSS | SCxCS | Branch-UQ (Branch-UQ not yet implemented). Perturbation style: self-correction | reflection | alt-path | verification (one active). Trigger: Wait-family | newline/sentence-boundary (one active). Model axes (Vocab/Scale/Context/Model/State/Arch/Attn): one impl per path by construction.",
        "",
        "**NEVER-SAME-PATH (audited, none found among model axes).** All Model/State/Arch/Attn/Vocab/Scale/Context impls compose by construction (that is what the existing combos exercise). Known would-break-if-unadapted cases are guarded by documented stand-ins, not exclusions: no-delimiter exit (stop+decode used, s13); JSON relevance scoring (keyword-overlap stand-in, s15); ACCL judge (stubbed, needs judge LLM, s15); full-batch MLP recipe vs minibatch transformer loop (documented deviation with consequence: higher seed variance, s16). Any future guaranteed-incompatible pair gets listed here with both sides named.",
        ""
      ]
    },
