        "        subs = [(qq, convmem_f1(aa, gold), convmem_subem(aa, gold)) for qq, aa in out[\"sub\"]]\n",
        "        recs.append({\"q\": q, \"gold\": gold, \"answer\": out[\"answer\"][:400],\n",
        "                   \"f1\": convmem_f1(out[\"answer\"], gold), \"subem\": convmem_subem(out[\"answer\"], gold),\n",
        "                   \"sub\": subs, \"trace\": convmem_trace([str(i) for i in range(len(docs))], q, [])})\n",
        "    summ = {\"n\": len(recs), \"mean_f1\": sum(r[\"f1\"] for r in recs) / max(1, len(recs)),\n",
        "            \"mean_subem\": sum(r[\"subem\"] for r in recs) / max(1, len(recs)), \"records\": recs}\n",
        "    _P(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P(out_path).write_text(_json4.dumps(summ, indent=2))\n",
        "    return summ\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Length note: why RULER 28k-896k never runs single-pass here, and what does instead",
        "",
        "Stated plainly: no ctx impl reaches 28k on quadratic attention - ctx2048 is the single-pass ceiling in this file, and 896k is ~440x beyond it. Two mechanisms cover the gap instead of pretending otherwise: (1) the ConvMem hierarchy (§15) is *itself* the long-context engine - an 8k kernel over 896k via O(log N) recursion, so RULER-scale evaluation runs *through* `convmem_run`, never through one context window; (2) sliding-window attention below extends the single-pass ceiling modestly and is registered as `Attn::slidingwindow` (header list appended; backing implementation here, promotion into the Attn Head paths is pending your call since those cells are yours). Length mapping used by runners: RULER-28k..896k est -> nanoGPT-NIAH at ctx*C scaled lengths with the same needle/distractor protocol - same method, honestly smaller lengths, never cited as RULER-scale numbers.",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT sliding-window attention (reference implementation) | Backs Attn::slidingwindow (header list appended; promotion into the user-owned Head paths pending owner call) | site: (B,H,T,hs) q/k/v -> causal local-window scores+context, drop-in for the two matmuls | plain codeblock, no wrapper edit to existing cells by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Causal sliding window: position i attends only to [i-window, i]. Same site and \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"shapes as q@kT and attn@v, so any Head can call these two functions instead. Cuts \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"single-pass memory from O(T^2) to O(T*window); extends the feasible window modestly \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"(not to RULER scale - the hierarchy covers that). Composes with all norms/arches; \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"alternative to full-context vanillaatten/mqa/gqa (pick 1 per path, s17 rule).\"\"\"\n",
        "def sliding_window_scores(q, k, window=64):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    B, H, T, hs = q.shape\n",
        "    s = q @ k.transpose(-2, -1) / (hs ** 0.5)\n",
        "    idx = _t.arange(T)\n",
        "    allow = (idx.unsqueeze(1) - idx.unsqueeze(0) >= 0) & (idx.unsqueeze(1) - idx.unsqueeze(0) < window)\n",
        "    return s.masked_fill(~allow.to(s.device), float(\"-inf\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "def sliding_window_context(attn_weights, v):\n",
        "    return attn_weights @ v\n",
        "\n",
        "def convmem_niah_at_scale(needles, distractors, queries, ctx_cap=512, W=200, S=40):\n",
        "    docs = convmem_build_niah([n for n, _ in needles], distractors)\n",
        "    text = \" \".join(docs)\n",
        "    scale_note = {\"protocol\": \"NIAH needle+distractors (paper App A)\",\n",
        "                \"lengths\": \"nanoGPT-scaled (ctx*C windows), NOT RULER 28k-896k\",\n",
        "                \"hierarchy_depth\": convmem_depth(len(text.split()), W)}\n",
        "    outs = []\n",
        "    for q, gold in queries:\n",
        "        outs.append((q, convmem_run(text, q, W, S)))\n",
        "    return {\"note\": scale_note, \"runs\": [(q, o[\"answer\"][:200]) for q, o in outs]}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 19. Geodesic Decoding \u2013 RiLM: Parameter-Efficient Language Modeling via Geodesic Decoding (Li 2026, arXiv:2609.10305; no public code found)",
        "",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** Below ~1M params, Wout (d x |V|) eats a third of the budget (Table I: 289k vs 776k/777k). RiLM deletes it: p(w|h) comes from -d_M(h,e_w)^2/tau over the SHARED embedding table (Eq.3), flat R^d (h+v steps) or Poincare ball (Mobius Eq.4, c=1.0 - naive exp_h collapses to uniform |V|, Table IX). Results: Hyp 54.2 WT-2 (~2x over SSM-tied 113.0, Table IV); Flat wins PTB 40.9 vs 69.8 (Table VI, curvature is validation-choice); 10k vocab persists ~2x (Table V); tied-math: -||h||^2 cancels in softmax so word NORMs carry the difference vs tying (sV.C). Scoped to controlled 2k-vocab comparisons (Table VIII warning).",
        "",
        "**Repo note:** anonymous supplement only, no public code (0 issues reviewable) - text-faithful. Integration reasoning (s17 rule): replacing lm_head changes the compiled model, so Flat geodesic decoding is a genuine Model Impl (same site as the Linear/AdderConvLinear lm_head: (B,T,emb)->(B,T,vocab) logits), following the RegularisedBN post-init swap precedent - no class duplication. Hyperbolic variant deferred (needs manifold stack: Mobius ops, ball projection, c=1.0, lr 3e-3, clip 1.0); flat-first is paper-justified (Table XI: compact corpora -> Flat; Shakespeare is compact). Tying constraint: the head MUST share token_embedding - a separate copy is a NEVER, it doubles params and breaks the design.",
        ""
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Model::geodesicflat{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"GeodesicFlat lm_head swap (Paper Eq.3, tau=1.0; Table I budget logic).\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Logits = -||h - E||^2 / tau computed against the SHARED token_embedding table; \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"no Wout allocated. Follows the RegularisedBN precedent: post-init submodule swap on \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"the live model object, so it composes with every Scale/Vocab/Context/State/Arch/Attn \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"path (shapes: (B,T,emb) -> (B,T,vocab)). NEVER a separate embedding copy.\"\"\"\n",
        "class GeodesicHead(torch.nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, token_embedding, tau=1.0):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.emb = token_embedding\n",
        "        self.tau = tau\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, h):\n",
        "        E = self.emb.weight\n",
        "        d2 = (h.unsqueeze(-2) - E.unsqueeze(0).unsqueeze(0)).pow(2).sum(-1)\n",
        "        return -d2 / self.tau\n",
        "\n",
        "model.lm_head = GeodesicHead(model.token_embedding, tau=1.0)\n",
        "n_wout = vocab_sz * model.token_embedding.weight.shape[1]\n",
        "n_params_tot = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
        "print(f\"geodesicflat: Wout params removed={n_wout}, total now={n_params_tot} (Table I analog)\")\n"
      ]
    }
    }@},
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT RiLM budget + smoke comparison | Paper Table I (param ledger), Table II (ctx64/bs128/ep10 schedule), sIV baselines | graded 07_Table1_Budget | plain codeblock (orchestrator), no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Param ledger for the live model (emb/Wout/core split) + tiny train-briefly-and-compare \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"harness: same data/steps for linear-head vs geodesic-head paths, reports val PPL + \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"params. Smoke-scale only (not the paper's 10-epoch protocol); decides whether the \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"geodesic claim visibly holds on nanoGPT before any serious budget is spent.\"\"\"\n",
        "def rilm_budget(model, vocab_sz):\n",
        "    d = model.token_embedding.weight.shape[1]\n",
        "    emb = d * vocab_sz\n",
        "    tot = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
        "    return {\"emb\": emb, \"wout\": 0 if isinstance(model.lm_head, GeodesicHead) else emb,\n",
        "            \"total\": tot, \"wout_frac\": (0.0 if isinstance(model.lm_head, GeodesicHead) else emb / max(1, tot))}\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_rilm_smoke_comparison(make_model_fn, get_batch_fn, steps=300, out_path=\"outputs/rilm_results.json\"):\n",
        "    import json as _json5\n",
        "    from pathlib import Path as _P\n",
        "    rec = {}\n",
        "    for name in (\"linear\", \"geodesic\"):\n",
        "        m = make_model_fn().to(device)\n",
        "        if name == \"geodesic\":\n",
        "            m.lm_head = GeodesicHead(m.token_embedding, tau=1.0)\n",
        "        opt = torch.optim.Adam(m.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
        "        lf = torch.nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
        "        m.train()\n",
        "        for s in range(steps):\n",
        "            xb, yb = get_batch_fn(\"train\")\n",
        "            xb, yb = xb.to(device), yb.to(device)\n",
        "            opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "            lf(m(xb).view(-1, m.lm_head.out_features if hasattr(m.lm_head, \"out_features\") else vocab_sz), yb.view(-1)).backward()\n",
        "            opt.step()\n",
        "        m.eval()\n",
        "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "            xb, yb = get_batch_fn(\"train\")\n",
        "            lv = lf(m(xb.to(device)).view(-1, vocab_sz), yb.to(device).view(-1)).item()\n",
        "        rec[name] = {\"loss\": lv, \"ppl\": float(torch.tensor(lv).exp()),\n",
        "                   \"budget\": rilm_budget(m, vocab_sz)}\n",
        "    _P(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P(out_path).write_text(_json5.dumps(rec, indent=2))\n",
        "    return rec\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Compatibility: RiLM: Parameter-Efficient Language Modeling via Geodesic Decoding (Li 2026, arXiv:2609.10305)",
        "",
        "- **STACK:** geodesic head + every Vocab (savings grow with |V|; head shares the table by construction) / Scale / Context / State / Arch / Attn path; budget cell + any live model; smoke runner + any get_batch; checkpoint probing tracks PPL either way.",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1):** lm_head Linear (matmul) | AdderConvLinear (addernetmatmul) | GeodesicHead (geodesicflat) - same site, same shapes; flat | hyp (hyp unimplemented: needs Mobius stack, ball projection, c=1.0/lr 3e-3/clip; Table IX collapse is the failure mode to re-test when built).",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** separate (untied) embedding copy alongside GeodesicHead (doubles params, breaks tying-constraint design); hyp Mobius ops applied to Euclidean states; Table VIII-style full-vocab leaderboard claims from 2k-vocab runs (paper's own warning).",
        "",
        "### Relations: RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)",
        "",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Flat-variant states stay Euclidean, so L2-LR/PLS probes apply unchanged - probe the geodesic model with the same heads. Hyp states would break probe geometry assumptions (non-Euclidean distances); probes on HypRiLM are untested by design.",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Confidence comes from the same softmax (geodesic logits feed Eq.4 math identically); CS/RSS arithmetic is decoder-agnostic. Untested combo, no shared state.",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): THEME LINK, no code path shared.** Both are param-scarcity stories (Wout budget pressure ~= capacity pressure); grokking clocks could track a geodesic-head run (norm dynamics under tying are unmeasured - open experiment).",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): NONE.** Different stages (readout geometry vs long-context scaffolding); no shared code path. Forced relations would be fake - recorded as none.",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): NONE beyond backbone.** GeodesicHead replaces the readout of whatever backbone path is live, including Attn:: variants (composition by design).",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT RiLM Fig.3 analog on live nanoGPT states | Paper Fig.3 (PCA paths, norm band, Table X top-5) + graded 07_Fig3_Geometry | uses s10 hook extractor + GeodesicHead or linear head | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Trajectory diagnostics for a live prefix: (a/b) 2D PCA of vocab cloud + state path \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"with h0/hT marked (Poincare circle drawn only for HypRiLM-style states); (c) ||h_t|| \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"per step with the paper's [0.29,0.71] band as reference (flat has no band - raw norms \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"reported); top-k continuations ranked by the live head (geodesic -d2 or linear logits).\"\"\"\n",
        "def rilm_trajectory_geometry(model, prefix_ids, topk=5):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    xb = _t.tensor([prefix_ids], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    feats = {}\n",
        "    hooks = [blk.register_forward_hook(lambda m, i, o, _k=len(feats): feats.setdefault(_k, o.detach())) for blk in model.blocks]\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        logits = model(xb)\n",
        "    for h in hooks:\n",
        "        h.remove()\n",
        "    H = feats[max(feats)].float().cpu()\n",
        "    E = model.token_embedding.weight.detach().float().cpu()\n",
        "    Xc = _t.cat([E, H[0]], dim=0) - _t.cat([E, H[0]], dim=0).mean(0, keepdim=True)\n",
        "    U, S, Vh = _t.linalg.svd(Xc, full_matrices=False)\n",
        "    Z = Xc @ Vh[:2].t()\n",
        "    Zv, Zp = Z[:len(E)], Z[len(E):]\n",
        "    norms = H[0].norm(dim=1).tolist()\n",
        "    k = min(topk, logits.shape[-1])\n",
        "    top = logits[0, -1, :].topk(k).indices.tolist()\n",
        "    geo = isinstance(model.lm_head, GeodesicHead)\n",
        "    return {\"vocab2d\": Zv[::max(1, len(E) // 300)].tolist(), \"path2d\": Zp.tolist(),\n",
        "            \"norms\": norms, \"band\": [0.29, 0.71],\n",
        "            \"in_band\": all(0.29 <= v <= 0.71 for v in norms) if geo else None,\n",
        "            \"topk\": top, \"head\": \"geodesic\" if geo else \"linear\"}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 20. Depth Pruning \u2013 Forward-Free LLM Depth Pruning via Weight Redundancy (Yun & Lim 2026, arXiv:2609.09883; no public code found)",
        "",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** Removing whole transformer blocks beats per-weight pruning for latency, but picking blocks usually needs calibration forwards (ShortGPT/Streamline/LoRP) or per-block magnitudes that ignore inter-layer relations (Mag+). WRP works from checkpoint weights alone: CKA similarity of centered attention-out + MLP-down Grams (Eq.1-2) averaged with 7-projection scale cosine (Eq.3) into S; spectral K in {2,4} from eigengaps vs depth-null (Eq.4-5); two-stage allocation protecting first/last. Results: +10.68-17.15 over Mag+ (avg 57.41 vs LoRP 57.93), best pruned avg on Qwen 8/40, selector GPU 0GB (Fig.1), -21-25% latency/memory at 25% cut (Fig.4).",
        "",
        "**Repo note:** the paper names no public code and search finds no implementation (0 issues reviewable) - text-faithful. Integration reasoning (s17 rule): pruning is post-training surgery on a live checkpoint, not a compile variant (Scale:: already covers build-time depth), so plain orchestrator cells, no new Techniques.",
        "",
        "**nanoGPT mapping (deviations documented, not hidden).** Wo^l = per-block MultiHead self_attn.proj (the attention-out projection); Wdown^l = FeedForward net[2] (the down projection). Scale vector uses SIX available projections (key/query/value per-head means + proj + net[0] + net[2]) - the paper's seven include a gate nanoGPT lacks. Spectral clustering via torch eigsh + fixed-seed k-means loop (paper: normalized-Laplacian embedding, fixed seed).",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT WRP descriptors + S matrix | Paper Eq.1 (center+Gram), Eq.2 (CKA, Sproj avg), Eq.3 (7-proj scale cosine w/ model-mean centering, S avg, diag 1), eps=1e-12 | graded 08_Equations | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Block descriptors from live nanoGPT weights (no forward passes, no calibration).\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Gram is permutation-invariant in intermediate dims; CKA normalizes scale; the \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"scale vector uses the six projections nanoGPT has (no gate - documented deviation).\"\"\"\n",
        "def wrp_gram(W):\n",
        "    d = W.shape[0]\n",
        "    Hd = torch.eye(d, device=W.device) - torch.ones(d, d, device=W.device) / d\n",
        "    Wf = Hd @ W.double()\n",
        "    return Wf @ Wf.t()\n",
        "\n",
        "def wrp_cka(Gi, Gj, eps=1e-12):\n",
        "    return float((Gi * Gj).sum() / (Gi.norm() * Gj.norm() + eps))\n",
        "\n",
        "def wrp_block_mats(model):\n",
        "    outs, downs, scales = [], [], []\n",
        "    for blk in model.blocks:\n",
        "        outs.append(blk.self_attn.proj.weight.detach())\n",
        "        downs.append(blk.ffwd.net[2].weight.detach())\n",
        "        qs = [h.query.weight.detach() for h in blk.self_attn.heads]\n",
        "        ks = [h.key.weight.detach() for h in blk.self_attn.heads]\n",
        "        vs = [h.value.weight.detach() for h in blk.self_attn.heads]\n",
        "        allm = qs + ks + vs + [blk.self_attn.proj.weight.detach(), blk.ffwd.net[0].weight.detach(), blk.ffwd.net[2].weight.detach()]\n",
        "        scales.append(torch.tensor([float(m.norm()) for m in allm]))\n",
        "    return outs, downs, torch.stack(scales)\n",
        "\n",
        "def wrp_similarity(model, eps=1e-12):\n",
        "    outs, downs, scales = wrp_block_mats(model)\n",
        "    L = len(outs)\n",
        "    Go = [wrp_gram(W) for W in outs]\n",
        "    Gd = [wrp_gram(W) for W in downs]\n",
        "    Sproj = torch.zeros(L, L)\n",
        "    for i in range(L):\n",
        "        for j in range(L):\n",
        "            Sproj[i, j] = (wrp_cka(Go[i], Go[j], eps) + wrp_cka(Gd[i], Gd[j], eps)) / 2\n",
        "    mu = scales.mean(0, keepdim=True)\n",
        "    fe = scales.double() - mu.double()\n",
        "    n = fe.norm(dim=1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(eps)\n",
        "    Sscale = (fe @ fe.t()) / (n @ n.t() + eps)\n",
        "    S = (Sproj.double() + Sscale) / 2\n",
        "    S.fill_diagonal_(1.0)\n",
        "    return S.float()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT WRP clustering + allocation + removal | Paper Eq.4 (Laplacian, d2/d3 vs depth-null S0, rho->K in {2,4}), Eq.5-adjacent r/rbar two-stage rule (first/last protected, rbar=-inf under 2 remaining, ties to lower index) + Mag+ baseline (per-block Frobenius, paper s4.1) | graded 08_Equations | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Spectral K-selection, k-means (fixed seed), two-stage removal, block surgery.\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Mag+ included in-cell as the comparison the paper centers on (beats it by 10-17 pts).\"\"\"\n",
        "def wrp_kmeans(X, K, seed=0, iters=50):\n",
        "    g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    C = X[torch.randperm(len(X), generator=g)[:K]].double()\n",
        "    for _ in range(iters):\n",
        "        d = ((X.double().unsqueeze(1) - C.unsqueeze(0)) ** 2).sum(-1)\n",
        "        a = d.argmin(1)\n",
        "        for k in range(K):\n",
        "            if (a == k).any():\n",
        "                C[k] = X.double()[a == k].mean(0)\n",
        "    return a.tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "def wrp_select(S, P, seed=0):\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    L = S.shape[0]\n",
        "    A = ((S.double() + 1) / 2).numpy()\n",
        "    _np.fill_diagonal(A, 1.0)\n",
        "    Dinv = _np.diag(1 / _np.sqrt(A.sum(1)))\n",
        "    Lmat = _np.eye(L) - Dinv @ A @ Dinv\n",
        "    eig = sorted(_np.linalg.eigvalsh(Lmat).tolist())\n",
        "    d2, d3 = eig[2] - eig[1], eig[3] - eig[2]\n",
        "    S0 = S.double().numpy().copy()\n",
        "    for i in range(L):\n",
        "        for j in range(L):\n",
        "            dd = abs(i - j)\n",
        "            S0[i, j] = S.double().numpy()[abs(_np.arange(L)[:, None] - _np.arange(L)) == dd].mean() if dd else 1.0\n",
        "    A0 = (S0 + 1) / 2\n",
        "    _np.fill_diagonal(A0, 1.0)\n",
        "    D0 = _np.diag(1 / _np.sqrt(A0.sum(1)))\n",
        "    e0 = sorted(_np.linalg.eigvalsh(_np.eye(L) - D0 @ A0 @ D0).tolist())\n",
        "    n2, n3 = e0[2] - e0[1], e0[3] - e0[2]\n",
        "    e2, e3 = max(d2 - n2, 0), max(d3 - n3, 0)\n",
        "    if e2 + e3 == 0:\n",
        "        K = 2\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        K = 2 if (e2 / (e2 + e3)) >= 0.5 else 4\n",
        "    K = min(K, L)\n",
        "    emb = _np.stack([_np.linalg.eigh(Lmat)[1][:, k] for k in range(K)], axis=1)\n",
        "    assign = wrp_kmeans(torch.tensor(emb, dtype=torch.float), K, seed)\n",
        "    clusters, order = {}, sorted(set(assign), key=lambda c: min(i for i, a in enumerate(assign) if a == c))\n",
        "    cmap = {c: k for k, c in enumerate(order)}\n",
        "    clusters = {k: [i for i, a in enumerate(assign) if cmap[a] == k] for k in range(len(order))}\n",
        "    Sm = S.double()\n",
        "    removed, remaining = [], {k: list(v) for k, v in clusters.items()}\n",
        "    eligible = lambda: [i for i in range(L) if i not in removed and i not in (0, L - 1)]\n",
        "    def r_of(i, members):\n",
        "        others = [m for m in members if m != i]\n",
        "        return sum(float(Sm[i, m]) for m in others) / max(1, len(others))\n",
        "    def rbar(members):\n",
        "        if len(members) < 2:\n",
        "            return float(\"-inf\")\n",
        "        s = sum(float(Sm[i, j]) for ii, i in enumerate(members) for j in members[ii + 1:])\n",
        "        return 2 * s / (len(members) * (len(members) - 1))\n",
        "    while len(removed) < P:\n",
        "        cands = [k for k in remaining if any(m in eligible() for m in remaining[k])]\n",
        "        if not cands:\n",
        "            break\n",
        "        if any(len(remaining[k]) == len(clusters[k]) for k in cands):\n",
        "            k = min([k for k in cands if len(remaining[k]) == len(clusters[k])])\n",
        "            pool = [m for m in remaining[k] if m in eligible()]\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            k = max(cands, key=lambda kk: (rbar(remaining[kk]), -kk))\n",
        "            pool = [m for m in remaining[k] if m in eligible()]\n",
        "        victim = min(pool, key=lambda m: (r_of(m, remaining[k]), m))\n",
        "        removed.append(victim)\n",
        "        remaining[k].remove(victim)\n",
        "    return sorted(removed), K, clusters\n",
        "\n",
        "def wrp_magplus(model, P):\n",
        "    scores = []\n",
        "    for li, blk in enumerate(model.blocks):\n",
        "        s = sum(p.detach().double().norm().item() for p in blk.parameters())\n",
        "        scores.append((s, li))\n",
        "    scores.sort()\n",
        "    return sorted([li for _, li in scores[:P]])\n",
        "\n",
        "def wrp_prune_blocks(model, remove):\n",
        "    keep = [b for i, b in enumerate(model.blocks) if i not in set(remove)]\n",
        "    model.blocks = torch.nn.Sequential(*keep)\n",
        "    return model, sorted(remove)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT WRP runner (claim-test on live nanoGPT) | Paper s4 (recovery-free eval; Fig.4 cost logic) + s3.2 baselines | graded 08_Table1_Main/08_Fig4_Cost | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Select via WRP (and Mag+ for the paper's head-to-head), prune copies, measure val \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"loss/PPL + params before/after. Recovery-free like the paper (no retraining after cut).\"\"\"\n",
        "import copy as _copy\n",
        "import json as _json6\n",
        "import time as _time6\n",
        "def run_wrp_benchmark(model, get_batch_fn, P=1, seed=0, out_path=\"outputs/wrp_results.json\"):\n",
        "    from pathlib import Path as _P\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    loss_fn = _t.nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
        "    S = wrp_similarity(model)\n",
        "    D, K, clusters = wrp_select(S, P, seed)\n",
        "    Dm = wrp_magplus(model, P)\n",
        "    def val_loss(m):\n",
        "        m.eval()\n",
        "        tot, n = 0.0, 0\n",
        "        with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "            for _ in range(5):\n",
        "                xb, yb = get_batch_fn(\"train\")\n",
        "                xb, yb = xb.to(dev), yb.to(dev)\n",
        "                out_dim = m.lm_head.out_features if hasattr(m.lm_head, \"out_features\") else vocab_sz\n",
        "                tot += loss_fn(m(xb).view(-1, out_dim), yb.view(-1)).item()\n",
        "                n += 1\n",
        "        return tot / max(1, n)\n",
        "    base_n = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
        "    base_loss = val_loss(model)\n",
        "    rec = {\"P\": P, \"K\": K, \"S_mean\": float(S.mean()), \"wrp_remove\": D, \"mag_remove\": Dm,\n",
        "           \"base\": {\"params\": base_n, \"loss\": base_loss}}\n",
        "    for name, rem in ((\"wrp\", D), (\"magplus\", Dm)):\n",
        "        m2 = _copy.deepcopy(model)\n",
        "        t0 = _time6.time()\n",
        "        wrp_prune_blocks(m2, rem)\n",
        "        dt = _time6.time() - t0\n",
        "        rec[name] = {\"params\": sum(p.numel() for p in m2.parameters()), \"loss\": val_loss(m2), \"select_s\": dt}\n",
        "    _P(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P(out_path).write_text(_json6.dumps(rec, indent=2))\n",
        "    return rec\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Compatibility: Forward-Free LLM Depth Pruning via Weight Redundancy (Yun & Lim 2026, arXiv:2609.09883)",
        "",
        "- **STACK:** selection + any trained checkpoint (reads weights only, zero GPU by construction); pruned model + checkpoint probing re-run, probe heads (fewer layers for LayerMix top-K - expected consequence: K clamps to depth), SABER exit (latency compounds with depth cut), ConvMem hierarchy over pruned backbone, grokking clocks on pruned runs, RiLM head untouched (not a block).",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1):** selector WRP | Mag+ | random per pruning decision (paper centers WRP-vs-Mag+); K auto {2,4} vs forced; P budget per run. Removal itself is destructive per copy - always prune a deepcopy, never the trained original.",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** pruning blocks 0 / L-1 (guarded: first+last protected); pruned-model numbers cited as dense-model numbers; Mag+ first-4+last-2 guard read as WRP's guard (different: first+last only).",
        "",
        "### Relations: WRP (arXiv:2609.09883) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)",
        "",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probes score pre/post-prune states with identical heads; LayerMix top-K clamps to surviving depth (consequence recorded). Pruning changes WHAT is probed, never the probe math.",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Pruned model still generates; RSS-gated exit applies unchanged; expect compounded latency wins (depth cut x early exit), untested combo.",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Clocks + norm tracker run on pruned checkpoints; norm-ratio band may shift under fewer blocks (open measurement, not assumed).",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** Hierarchy runs over a pruned backbone (fewer, cheaper kernel calls); skip-buffer r=2 logic untouched by depth.",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): NONE beyond sharing the object.** Head is not a block: WRP never selects it, GeodesicHead works identically pre/post prune (composition by design).",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): NONE.** Pruning consumes whatever backbone path is live, including Attn:: variants.",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 21. Prefix Optimization \u2013 Beyond Confidence: Stability-Aware Test-Time Adaptation for LLM Reasoning (Gu et al. 2026, arXiv:2609.11393; no public code found)",
        "",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** Confidence-only test-time optimization steers into fragile high-confidence states. TASCO optimizes a shared continuous prefix V (LxD) on the frozen LLM for confidence + stability: Lconf = mean token entropy (Eq.1); Random Perturbation re-decodes under K=8 Gaussian prefixes (sigma=0.01), penalizes sample variance S (Eq.4), LRP=Lconf+lam*Lrand (Eq.5, lam=20/5); Sharpness-Aware Perturbation takes one gradient step eps*=rho*g/||g|| (rho=0.8, Eq.8) with stop-grad LSAP (Eq.9). Results: +14.4/+17.2/+2.9 general (Table 1), +6.8/+6.0 reasoning (Table 2), -28%/-24% tokens (Fig.4), transfer without re-optimization (Fig.6); theory bounds both objectives (Props 1-4).",
        "",
        "**Repo note:** no public code found (aggregators: no code link; 0 issues reviewable) - text-faithful. Integration reasoning (s17 rule): V is runtime input (nn.Parameter OUTSIDE the model, backbone frozen), so plain orchestrator cells, no new Techniques. RP vs SAP is the genuine ALTERNATIVE here (same site: the prefix update - pick 1 per run). Config constraint: L + query length must fit ctx_len (small-ctx paths shrink L).",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT TASCO prefix machinery | Paper s3 Preliminaries (V in R^{LxD}, E'=[V;E(X)], Eq.1 Lconf) + App A (N(0,I)/empirical init, AdamW on V only, tokens fixed during backprop) | graded 09_Equations | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Learnable prefix prepended at embedding level; model weights never touched.\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Positions continue past the prefix (documented choice; paper prepends V before E(X) \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"identically). Lconf = mean token entropy over generated tokens (Eq.1).\"\"\"\n",
        "class TascoPrefix(torch.nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, L, emb_dim, init=\"normal\", ref_emb=None):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        if init == \"empirical\" and ref_emb is not None:\n",
        "            mu, sd = ref_emb.mean(0), ref_emb.std(0).clamp_min(1e-6)\n",
        "            V0 = mu.unsqueeze(0) + sd.unsqueeze(0) * torch.randn(L, emb_dim)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            V0 = torch.randn(L, emb_dim)\n",
        "        self.V = torch.nn.Parameter(V0)\n",
        "\n",
        "def tasco_embed_with_prefix(model, ids, prefix):\n",
        "    tok = model.token_embedding(ids)\n",
        "    pos = model.position_embedding(torch.arange(tok.shape[1], device=tok.device).unsqueeze(0))\n",
        "    V = prefix.V.unsqueeze(0).expand(tok.shape[0], -1, -1)\n",
        "    return torch.cat([V, tok + pos], dim=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "def tasco_conf_entropy(model, prefix, ids, n_gen=16, temp=0.7):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    h = tasco_embed_with_prefix(model, ids.to(dev), prefix)\n",
        "    ents = []\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        for _ in range(n_gen):\n",
        "            x = h[:, -model.ctx_len:, :]\n",
        "            lg = model.blocks(x)\n",
        "            lg = model.ln_final(lg)\n",
        "            lg = model.lm_head(lg[:, -1:, :])\n",
        "            pr = _t.softmax(lg.squeeze(1) / max(temp, 1e-6), dim=-1)\n",
        "            ents.append(float(-(pr * pr.clamp_min(1e-12).log()).sum(1).mean()))\n",
        "            nx = _t.multinomial(pr.cpu(), 1).to(dev)\n",
        "            hn = model.token_embedding(nx) + model.position_embedding(_t.tensor([[h.shape[1] % model.ctx_len]], device=dev))\n",
        "            h = _t.cat([h, hn], dim=1)\n",
        "    return sum(ents) / max(1, len(ents))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT TASCO-RP (Random Perturbation) | Paper Eq.2-5 (K draws, c^(k) avg-loglik, S sample var, LRP; K=8/sigma=0.01/lam=20-5, App A) + Props 1-2 (unbiasedness, total-variance split) | graded 09_Equations | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Distributional stability: K Gaussian prefixes, greedy re-decode each, penalize Var.\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"ALTERNATIVE to SAP (same site: the prefix update - pick 1 per run). Costs K re-decodes.\"\"\"\n",
        "def tasco_teacher_loglik(model, prefix, ids, toks):\n",
        "    h = tasco_embed_with_prefix(model, ids.to(next(model.parameters()).device), prefix)\n",
        "    x = h[:, -model.ctx_len:, :]\n",
        "    lg = model.lm_head(model.ln_final(model.blocks(x)))\n",
        "    L = toks.shape[1]\n",
        "    lp = torch.log_softmax(lg[:, -L:, :], dim=-1)\n",
        "    return lp.gather(-1, toks.unsqueeze(-1)).squeeze(-1).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "def tasco_rp_loss(model, prefix, ids, toks, K=8, sigma=0.01, lam_rand=20.0):\n",
        "    c0 = tasco_teacher_loglik(model, prefix, ids, toks)\n",
        "    cs = []\n",
        "    for _ in range(K):\n",
        "        eps = sigma * torch.randn_like(prefix.V)\n",
        "        Vsave = prefix.V.detach().clone()\n",
        "        prefix.V.data.add_(eps)\n",
        "        cs.append(tasco_teacher_loglik(model, prefix, ids, toks))\n",
        "        prefix.V.data.copy_(Vsave)\n",
        "    S = sum((c - sum(cs) / len(cs)) ** 2 for c in cs) / max(1, len(cs) - 1)\n",
        "    return -c0 + lam_rand * S, -float(c0.detach()), float(S.detach())\n",
        "\n",
        "def tasco_rp_step(model, prefix, ids, opt, K=8, sigma=0.01, lam_rand=20.0, n_gen=16):\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "        h = tasco_embed_with_prefix(model, ids.to(dev), prefix)\n",
        "        toks = []\n",
        "        hh = h\n",
        "        for _ in range(n_gen):\n",
        "            x = hh[:, -model.ctx_len:, :]\n",
        "            lg = model.lm_head(model.ln_final(model.blocks(x))[:, -1:, :])\n",
        "            nx = lg.squeeze(1).argmax(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "            toks.append(nx)\n",
        "            hn = model.token_embedding(nx) + model.position_embedding(torch.tensor([[hh.shape[1] % model.ctx_len]], device=dev))\n",
        "            hh = torch.cat([hh, hn], dim=1)\n",
        "        toks = torch.cat(toks, dim=1)\n",
        "    opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "    loss, base, S = tasco_rp_loss(model, prefix, ids, toks, K, sigma, lam_rand)\n",
        "    loss.backward()\n",
        "    opt.step()\n",
        "    return float(loss.detach()), base, S\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT TASCO-SAP (Sharpness-Aware Perturbation) | Paper Eq.6-9 (min-max rho-ball rho=0.8, g, eps*=rho*g/||g||, LSAP + stop-grad) + Props 3-4 (O(rho^2) bounds, stationary curvature) | graded 09_Equations | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Worst-case stability: one gradient-guided perturbation on the fixed trajectory.\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"ALTERNATIVE to RP (same site - pick 1 per run). One extra eval, no K re-decodes.\"\"\"\n",
        "def tasco_sap_eps(grad, rho=0.8):\n",
        "    n = float(grad.norm())\n",
        "    return grad.new_zeros(grad.shape) if n == 0 else rho * grad / n\n",
        "\n",
        "def tasco_sap_step(model, prefix, ids, opt, rho=0.8, n_gen=16):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    prefix.V.requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    h = tasco_embed_with_prefix(model, ids.to(dev), prefix)\n",
        "    x = h[:, -model.ctx_len:, :]\n",
        "    lg = model.lm_head(model.ln_final(model.blocks(x))[:, -1:, :])\n",
        "    pr = _t.softmax(lg.squeeze(1), dim=-1)\n",
        "    ent = -(pr * pr.clamp_min(1e-12).log()).sum(1).mean()\n",
        "    g = _t.autograd.grad(ent, prefix.V, retain_graph=False)[0].detach()\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        prefix.V.add_(tasco_sap_eps(g, rho))\n",
        "    h2 = tasco_embed_with_prefix(model, ids.to(dev), prefix)\n",
        "    x2 = h2[:, -model.ctx_len:, :]\n",
        "    lg2 = model.lm_head(model.ln_final(model.blocks(x2))[:, -1:, :])\n",
        "    pr2 = _t.softmax(lg2.squeeze(1), dim=-1)\n",
        "    ent2 = -(pr2 * pr2.clamp_min(1e-12).log()).sum(1).mean()\n",
        "    opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "    ent2.backward()\n",
        "    opt.step()\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        prefix.V.sub_(tasco_sap_eps(g, rho))\n",
        "    return float(ent2.detach())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: TASCO end-to-end | Optimizes prefix (RP or SAP), grades boxed answers, emits outputs/tasco_results.json | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Few-epoch prefix adaptation on reasoning tasks, then greedy evaluation. Model frozen.\"\"\"\n",
        "import json as _json7\n",
        "def run_tasco_benchmark(model, tasks, variant=\"rp\", L=8, epochs=3, out_path=\"outputs/tasco_results.json\"):\n",
        "    from pathlib import Path as _P\n",
        "    emb_dim = model.token_embedding.weight.shape[1]\n",
        "    prefix = TascoPrefix(L, emb_dim).to(next(model.parameters()).device)\n",
        "    opt = torch.optim.AdamW([prefix.V], lr=1e-3)\n",
        "    for ep in range(epochs):\n",
        "        for t in tasks:\n",
        "            ids = torch.tensor([encode(t[\"q\"][-model.ctx_len:])], dtype=torch.long)\n",
        "            if variant == \"rp\":\n",
        "                tasco_rp_step(model, prefix, ids, opt)\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                tasco_sap_step(model, prefix, ids, opt)\n",
        "    recs = []\n",
        "    for t in tasks:\n",
        "        ids = torch.tensor([encode(t[\"q\"][-model.ctx_len:])], dtype=torch.long)\n",
        "        out_ids, _ = saber_generate_early_exit(model, encode, decode, ids[0].tolist(), k=2, max_steps=20)\n",
        "        ans = saber_extract_boxed(decode(out_ids))\n",
        "        recs.append({\"q\": t[\"q\"][:60], \"pred\": ans, \"gold\": t[\"a\"], \"ok\": saber_grade(ans, t[\"a\"])})\n",
        "    acc = sum(r[\"ok\"] for r in recs) / max(1, len(recs))\n",
        "    out = {\"variant\": variant, \"L\": L, \"epochs\": epochs, \"acc\": acc, \"records\": recs}\n",
        "    _P(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P(out_path).write_text(_json7.dumps(out, indent=2))\n",
        "    return out\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Compatibility: Beyond Confidence: Stability-Aware Test-Time Adaptation for LLM Reasoning (Gu et al. 2026, arXiv:2609.11393)",
        "",
        "- **STACK:** prefix optimization + SABER exit (steered generations still exitable - closest relation in the file); + LayerMix probes (prefix-steered states remain probeable); + ConvMem hierarchy (prefix could prepend kernel inputs, untested); overhead-style accounting shared with s13/s18 runners.",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1):** RP | SAP per run (same site: the prefix update; RP costs K re-decodes, SAP one grad eval); confidence-only as ablation control (not a contender).",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** L + query length exceeding ctx_len (config constraint - small-ctx paths shrink L); model-weight updates alongside prefix updates (frozen-by-design; unfreezing changes the method into fine-tuning).",
        "",
        "### Relations: TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)",
        "",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (closest).** Same stability-under-perturbation theme, complementary stages: TASCO optimizes the prefix OFFLINE before generation, SABER exits ONLINE during generation. RP/SAP vs SC/CS are different operationalizations - never compared as same-site alternatives.",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Prefix-steered frozen states are still states; all probe heads apply unchanged. Stability-variance diagnostics (Table 3 analog) can reuse cv_auroc_for_probe machinery.",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): NONE.** Different phases (test-time adaptation vs training dynamics); no shared code path.",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (untested).** Learned prefix could prepend every kernel call's input; hierarchy math untouched.",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): NONE.** Readout geometry orthogonal to input steering.",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): NONE.** Pruning consumes checkpoints; prefix optimization consumes a live model. Independent stages.",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): NONE.** Works with whatever backbone path is live.",
